            "review_title": "Review at O Tinh House",
            "review_text": "terri_hugh\n32 contributions\n0\nAmazing place to eat in Saigon!\nMar 2025 • Couples\nAfter a long day of touring, we were tired, and also needed to pack for our trip home early in the morning. We checked our google map, and saw that this place had good reviews, and was an easy walk from our hotel. Talk about an amazing last meal for our visit to Vietnam! We tried the jackfruit with pesto sauce, the snakehead soup (wow!), and lemongrass chicken with thin little rice cakes, plus we each had amazing cocktails (a Smokey Negroni for me, and that really cool drink with the chili for my husband); our server was sweet, kind, and spoke great English (all the staff did, and we did our best with our limited Vietnamese); we had the opportunity to visit with the owner, who told us the story of how this place came to be, and he had returned to his roots; so great to chat with him, and with the two Italian ladies seated next to us; we left happy, full, and completely blissed out!\nRead more\nWritten March 25, 2025",
